  "worked_solution": "Since $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. So, the coefficients of $a$ must be equal, and the coefficients of $b$ must be equal.\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3\\lambda -\\mu =1 \\\\ \\lambda -4\\mu =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\mu =3\\lambda -1\n$$\n\nSubstituting back into the second equation, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda -4\\mu  & =2 \\\\ \\lambda -4(3\\lambda -1) & =2 \\\\ \\lambda -12\\lambda +4 & =2 \\\\ -11\\lambda  & =-2 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\frac{2}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =3\\lambda -1 \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{2}{11}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
